From 5265b15cef9bc3c72d06495516d7ceb7e80e0562 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZeroCode321 <ZeroCode321@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:20:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(conversation): declare a turn-status icon seat and ship
 the whale as a plugin
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`conversation.chat.turnStatusIcon` is a single, session-scoped seat beside the
running turn status. Unoccupied it renders nothing, so the status keeps its
text-only footprint and a deployment can drop the whale without touching this
package.

The whale itself is no longer a built-in row: it ships as a standalone plugin
package (dsh-whale-diving) that a profile installs, which is what makes it
manageable from the chest — install, uninstall, reorder, export, delete.
